 QuaRot is treated as a preprocessing/rotation transform (Hadamard applied to weights offline and to activations online) that is orthogonal to the rounding method — so it must be crossed with both baselines, not just GPTQ, to attribute gains. Include FP16/BF16 reference and (optionally) W8A8? No—weight-only. Include group-size matched comparison so effective bits are identical across methods (critical confounder: GPTQ often reported with g=128 while RTN per-channel; must equalize).\n- Metrics: primary = WikiText-2 perplexity (seq len 2048, non-overlapping) + C4 validation perplexity; secondary = zero-shot accuracy suite (e.g., lm-eval-harness: PIQA, ARC-e, HellaSwag, WinoGrande, LAMBADA, ARC-c) as mean and per-task; delta vs FP16 as a normalized degradation metric (e.g., ppl ratio and accuracy drop), and \"collapse indicator\" (perplexity > threshold, e.g., > 2× FP16 or > 100) to answer the \"stabilize\" part. Diagnostic proxies: per-layer quantization MSE / relative error, KL divergence between quantized and FP16 next-token distributions, and outlier statistics (max/median |w|, kurtosis) before/after Hadamard — these are cheap, low-variance, and directly measure the smoothing mechanism. Also report the theoretical smoothness metric used by rotation literature (e.g., coherence/flatness of the transformed matrix), computed offline as a pure-math check.\n- Controls: identical checkpoints/tokenizer; identical calibration set, size and seed (GPTQ needs calibration, RTN doesn't — but we must still control: same 128×2048-token C4 sequences used to pick GPTQ scales/Hessians AND to pick any QuaRot-related choices like which layers/whether to skip outliers, so no method gets extra data); identical group size and bits; identical excluded layers (embeddings, lm_head, first/last block) across all arms — QuaRot must not be allowed to \"cheat\" by keeping more layers in FP16; single-rotation determinism (fixed random Hadamard seeds, save the rotation matrices so all methods share exactly the same H); same hardware/precision of the quantization math (do GPTQ Hessian accumulation in fp32 for all arms); no activation/KV quantization at all (weight-only track), so QuaRot's online activation and K-V rotations must be either disabled or fused offline (they cancel mathematically: H·Hᵀ=I) — this is the single most important design detail for a weight-only claim, and it must be made explicit: in weight-only mode the online Hadamards are folded/cancelled, only the offline weight rotations + the compensating invariances (e.g., rotating W_down and W_up/W_gate jointly, or applying H to W after fusing LayerNorm) change anything. Actually in QuaRot, R1/R2/R3/R4 rotations keep the network mathematically invariant; for weight-only, applying the rotation changes the rounding grid of each matrix while leaving the exact FP function unchanged → the effect is purely \"better-conditioned rounding\", which is exactly the hypothesis we want to isolate. Good, state that.\n- Design of the \"stabilization\" question: pre-register thresholds; require ≥2 model scales (e.g., 7B and 13B/70B) and ≥2 families (LLaMA-2/3; OPT as secondary, given OPT historically has fewer outliers → helps falsify a family-specific effect). Seed variance only from stochastic elements (random Hadamard, GPTQ permutation order, calibration sampling); report 3 seeds where stochastic, and note perplexity on a fixed eval set is deterministic given checkpoint.\n- Deliverable: protocol + config files (YAML per arm) + code skeleton referencing upstream QuaRot/GPTQ implementations + analysis notebook template + pre-registered decision rule. No numbers.\n\n3) Assumptions (mark SUPUESTO) + uncertainties + consequential questions for researcher (topics: setup_5/7/11/16/17 — I can ask up to 6 questions; I'll propose the questions but the researcher asked only for plan, so I list them as questions to resolve next turn).\n\nI should ask which topics to query. Actually researcher_topics are given; the question_budget is 6. The researcher said \"solo inspección y propuesta\". So I'll list proposed clarifying questions but not consume them yet — or note them.\n\nAlso flag: QuaRot paper reports 4-bit W4A4KV4; at 2-bit weight-only the paper does not evaluate (uncertainty: extrapolation), so we must not cite 2-bit QuaRot numbers as paper evidence.\n\nLet me also note a factual caution: QuaRot's core evaluation is W4A4KV4 (4-bit weights, activations, KV cache); weight-only low-bit is a different regime, and whether rotation helps weight-only rounding is the actual open question — good framing.\n\nLet me write the handoff. Keep it organized, in Spanish, with clear SUPUESTO markers. Provide evidence section with the concrete command outputs.\n\nLength: reasonably detailed but the researcher asked for brevity (1 paragraph per point). I'll be structured but not bloated.\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"stage": "plan", "answer": "## 1) INSPECCIÓN INICIAL (nada pesado ejecutado; solo `ls`, `find`, chequeos de import)\n\n**Contenido de /workspace.** Exactamente un archivo: `/workspace/task.json` (579 B). No hay repositorios, ni scripts `.py`, ni notebooks, ni `requirements.txt`/`environment.yml`, ni configs YAML, ni carpeta `data/`, ni checkpoints. `du -sh /workspace` = 8.0K. Un `find` en todo el filesystem por `*quarot*`, `*gptq*`, `*llama*`, `*wikitext*`, `track.md` devuelve **cero coincidencias**. `track.md` no existe como archivo: es solo un campo embebido dentro de `task.json` → `\"documents\": {\"track.md\": \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\"}`.\n\n**Modelos y datasets.** Nada real. `environment.datasets = []`; no hay `/home/actor/.cache` ni `~/.cache` (HOME sin caché de HuggingFace); no hay variables `HF_HOME`/`HF_TOKEN`/proxy. Por tanto **LLaMA-2/LLaMA-3, OPT, WikiText-2 y C4 NO están presentes ni referenciados en el repo**: cualquier mención en el diseño es nominal (a nombre, a confirmar), no un artefacto