ttention scores q k^T invariant: q' = q R2... let me not go overboard; I'll present the table at the level of \"which rotation acts on which weight matrix's quantization grid, and whether it can be folded offline (weights only) or must be applied online (activations/cache)\".\n\nFor the design deliverable, the traceability table can be per-arm:\n\n| Rotation | Applied to | Weight-only status | Justification |\n- R1 (residual stream, d_model): foldable offline (Emb, W_q/k/v/up/gate input side; W_o/W_down output side; RMSNorm commutes) → KEEP-OFFLINE; affects quantization grid for W_q,W_k,W_v,W_up,W_gate (input dim). For W_o,W_down the R1 acts on output dim → doesn't change group-along-input difficulty but changes values; keep for invariance.\n- R2 (V head, d_h block-diag): affects grid of W_v (input dim? no, R2 applies to V output/head dim) → output-side → no grid change for W_v; but it enters W_o's input side (o_proj input includes v head dim) → affects W_o grid? In weight-only, K/V cache is FP16, so R2/R3 exist only to preserve invariance when the cache is quantized → ANULADO (H H^T = I) with a note that W_o's input rotation for v-part is instead handled by R4 (whole-head rotation of attention output), which subsumes R2 when R2=R4's block. In QuaRot, R4 is applied to attention output (i.e., o_proj input side) and R2 to V weights; the identity is v = xW_v R2 and then o_proj input includes rotated v through attention output... Actually attention output = P·V where V is the cache; if V' = V R2 then attn_out' = attn_out R2 (per head) → o_proj input rotated by (⊕_h R2) = R4 → so R4 = R2 ⊗ heads is exactly the induced rotation, meaning W_o must be quantized as W_o (⊕R2) with the online compensation being free (it's automatic since attention output is already rotated). Beautiful: so in weight-only, if we keep R2 on V weights, the o_proj input side is automatically rotated and we must fold R2^T into W_o's v-block — and no online op needed. But then quantizing W_o after fol